dist.ini has 'authority = cpan:JLMARTIN'. Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY (installed at /home/getty/perl5/lib/perl5/Dist/Zilla/PluginBundle/Author/GETTY.pm line 61) unconditionally prepends 'cpan:' to whatever the authority payload option holds: return 'cpan:'.$self->payload->{authority} if $self->payload->{authority};. Because dist.ini already includes the 'cpan:' prefix, the built META.json ends up with x_authority: "cpan:cpan:JLMARTIN" -- confirmed both in a fresh 'dzil build' of this working tree and in the already-released IO-K8s-1.107.tar.gz pulled from CPAN (GETTY/IO-K8s-1.107.tar.gz), so this is not new to 1.108 -- it has shipped broken in every release to date. The bundle's own POD documents the option as bare, e.g. 'authority = ETHER' (no cpan: prefix). Fix: dist.ini should read 'authority = JLMARTIN' (bare), which the bundle will correctly turn into cpan:JLMARTIN. Malformed x_authority undermines the very point of a co-maintained dist -- it doesn't match cpan:JLMARTIN so authority-aware tooling can't confirm JLMARTIN's claim. Not a blocker for 1.108 specifically (pre-existing, hasn't stopped any prior release) but worth fixing now that it's identified. Found during pre-1.108 release audit.

2026-09-01 19:51 dist.ini authority line now reads 'JLMARTIN' (bare); bundle will prepend cpan: → META.json x_authority becomes cpan:JLMARTIN. Verified with 'dzil build' on the modified dist.ini: built IO-K8s-1.108/META.json now contains "x_authority" : "cpan:JLMARTIN" (single prefix, was cpan:cpan:JLMARTIN before). Build artifacts cleaned.

